to-nat-friedman-source : List Word
to-nat-friedman-source = lines-of (cons "# Nat Friedman"
  (cons ""
  (cons "You have spent twenty-five years building the places where programmers' work adds up: GNOME and Ximian, Mono and Xamarin, then GitHub, the commons where most of the world's code now lives. You put Copilot into it. In 2023 you read about the Herculaneum papyri, found Brent Seales's scanning work, and when the founders you invited to fund it stayed quiet, you funded it yourself. You wrote the prize so that anyone's partial progress had to be open-sourced and so accrued to everyone. Three young programmers then read Philodemus out of a carbonized scroll. In 2025 you joined Meta to co-lead its Superintelligence Labs with Alexandr Wang. This page asks you to read hyperactivity the way you read the Seales papers: looking for the thing everyone else in the room has missed. Each claim below about Avik Jain's work links to the block of his paper, *hyperactivity*, Part I, that states it."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## What you saw that the field did not"
  (cons ""
  (cons "The papyrologists' working assumption was that the scrolls could not be opened. You concluded that the remaining problem was software, which meant anyone with a laptop could attack it. Most of a field's apparent difficulty is the field's own framing, and an outsider receptive to the experts' real results, but not bound by their assumptions, can see the problem's true shape. Your stated beliefs carry the same structure: speed buys feedback from reality, much of what people believe is wrong, and the work is to raise the ceiling."
  (cons ""
  (cons "The design of the Vesuvius prizes deserves more credit than it gets. The progress prizes required open-sourcing, so a contestant's small step became a step for every contestant. What you built was a mechanism for making many people's partial knowledge compose into one result."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## What hyperactivity is, in those terms"
  (cons ""
  (cons "In Avik's words, hyperactivity is “a language and a computational model of reality i.e. wolfram's ruliad executing on silicon”. Its core is the CCHM cubical calculus with clock-indexed guarded computation"
  (cons (cite s1-1-p4 "(§1.1)")
  (cons ", and a routine, its requirement and the reasoning that establishes it are terms of one language"
  (cons (cite s1-p25 "(1.5)")
  (cons "."
  (cons ""
  (cons "**GitHub, carried further.** GitHub made code shareable by name and history. In hyperactivity a definition is a content-addressed object with its typed syntax and dependency references, and a name is a view of it, so renaming does not rewrite the computation"
  (cons (cite s10-8-p2 "(§10.8)")
  (cons ". An equivalence gives a path, and transport along it carries the constructions that depend on one representation to the other"
  (cons (cite s1-p27 "(§1)")
  (cons ". An edit is a function on checked code, accompanied where required by a semantic relation between its input and output"
  (cons (cite s10-9-p3 "(§10.9)")
  (cons "."
  (cons ""
  (cons "**The Vesuvius mechanism, made structural.** Your progress prizes made partial results accrue to everyone by contract. Here a peer sends a definition with its dependency closure and proofs, and the recipient checks and uses it in its own context: communication makes a construction available for further computation"
  (cons (cite s10-8-p7 "(§10.8)")
  (cons ". A result stays usable exactly where its recorded dependencies still hold"
  (cons (cite s1-p30 "(§1)")
  (cons "."
  (cons ""
  (cons "**Copilot, and the step past it.** Copilot completes code by likeness to code it has seen. Avik holds that the end state of artificial intelligence is logic: symbolic reasoning over equality and higher paths. In this language a transformation's results are admitted through the same checking relation as ordinary definitions"
  (cons (cite s1-2-p2 "(§1.2)")
  (cons ", so a generated unit is admitted with its evidence or not at all. Since you now work on superintelligence, this is the part most worth your attention."
  (cons ""
  (cons "**Speed as feedback from reality.** Tests observe selected executions, whereas the reasoning term concerns every input in its stated domain"
  (cons (cite s1-p26 "(§1)")
  (cons ". The feedback you want from reality arrives as the checker's verdict over the whole domain, not a sample of it."
  (cons ""
  (cons "**Reading lost texts.** The scrolls were knowledge cut off from its readers. In the paper, language belongs inside the history under investigation, and a word opens onto the inherited activity of the human superorganism"
  (cons (cite s1-p17 "(§1)")
  (cons "; a display is a chosen observation of the computation, not its privileged source"
  (cons (cite s10-9-p6 "(§10.9)")
  (cons ". A recovered text enters the graph as units whose dependencies are real edges, not strings."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## Why you"
  (cons ""
  (cons "You funded the scrolls because the experts' consensus was that they could not be opened, and you did not accept that. That is the receptivity this work asks for: depth taken from experts and none of their limits. Avik turned down Jane Street and OpenAI to build this, and it has the shape you look for: a large amount of value, recoverable now, that the field's framing hides."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## Credit"
  (cons ""
  (cons "The open, composable commons this work assumes is in large part what you built: GNOME's community, Mono's openness, Xamarin, GitHub, and the prize design that made the scrolls a public effort. Wherever hyperactivity relies on those, you have full credit for them. Read this page looking for the best in it."
  (cons ""
  (cons "## Sources"
  (cons ""
  (cons "- Nat Friedman, Wikipedia, https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nat_Friedman"
  (cons "- Vesuvius Challenge grand prize, https://scrollprize.org/grandprize"
  (cons "- Interview with Nat Friedman on the scrolls, https://costofglory.substack.com/p/mysteries-of-the-scrolls"
  (cons "- Scientific American, a Herculaneum scroll unrolled in full, https://www.scientificamerican.com/article/ancient-roman-scrolls-destroyed-by-mount-vesuvius-digitally-unrolled-in-full-for-first-time/"
  (cons "- Friedman's stated beliefs, https://clippings.devonzuegel.com/post/nat-friedman-2"
  (cons "- Avik Jain, hyperactivity, Part I, the blocks linked above"
  nil))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))
